# The sites database is hashed byte for byte: `db_meta.json` carries a sha256 of
# `data.json`, and the client refuses a downloaded database whose hash does not
# match, so it keeps serving its old cache instead. A checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true`, the default on a Windows install of git, would rewrite
# every one of the file's ~130 000 newlines and change that hash, which breaks
# the agreement test added in #3419 for the contributor and, once such a file is
# committed, the auto-update for everyone.
maigret/resources/data.json -text
